  "description": "Scale, reposition and rotate a source image within its original canvas. Zoom 10–400%; Rotation −180° to +180° about the pixel-grid centre (clockwise positive); Position X/Y translate in canvas axes after rotation. Canvas Mode 0 repeats the image, Mode 1 flattens it against opaque black, and Mode 2 makes uncovered areas transparent. Mirror Tiles flips alternate tiles; Smooth Sampling selects bilinear or crisp nearest-neighbour sampling; Edge Softness adds a 0–8 px feather to non-tiled artwork edges. Both sampled RGB and alpha follow the same inverse rotation. The GPU-oriented repeat-smooth branch uses one bilinear source read per channel instead of four wrapped neighbours: this retains every source pixel and the source dimensions in a tile, but bilinear interpolation clamps inside each tile rather than blending its final pixel into the next tile across the edge. Visible seams may therefore remain in non-seamless input images. Nearest repeat and mirror tiling use full-image periods, and other non-tiled modes retain the original geometry and alpha behaviour. Strong downscaling uses bilinear rather than true mipmap/area filtering and may alias.",
